      "name": "CURRENTREDRAW"
    }
  ],
  "basis": [
    "Attempt-05 directly compared the same fixture/config in two isolated Native v24 runs and one pinned public-pyz run; manifest, seal, runtime pins, and raw/decoded logs were verified.",
    "For REDRAW -1, REDRAW 2, and helper-returned 2, Native CURRENTREDRAW returned 1, 0, 0 while the public pyz returned -1, 2, 2 through both expression and method-as-command routes.",
    "The nonconstant helper was evaluated once, sentinels were preserved, and each run reached REDRAW_BITS_DONE. Native source explains bit-0 normalization and the getter mapping; public source stores and returns the raw integer.",
    "Two independent reviewers accepted this finite difference scope. Earlier 0/1 matches remain valid only for their original scope. No product code was changed."
  ],
  "not_claimed": [
    "No full Int64-domain, invalid-expression, error-side-effect, or all evaluation-pattern claim.",
    "No rendered-pixel, redraw-timing, or frame-behavior comparison.",
    "Native natural process exit and exit code were not observed."
  ],
